From 0e437dc01f2ba961d5cf29bfe277367236893ccb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 22:07:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] v2.5.3: code-review correctness fixes + nav/header
 standardization

reaper_fw.c: admin-management RETURN scoped to INPUT (was also emitted on
FORWARD/OUTPUT, exempting the admin address's forwarded :443/:22 from the whole
firewall); port-forward external port now rejects empty/comma (rfw_valid_ports
permits both but --dport has no -m multiport), internal-port guard rejects empty.

gatekeeper.c, rwarden.c: apply.sh generated atomically (temp+rename) so a
concurrent restart_firewall cannot exec a half-written teardown. reaper_fw
already had this; GK and Warden did not.

rwarden.c: shared flock between fold.sh and stats.sh so a 30s poll straddling
the 15-min checkpoint cannot read the banked total before the mv and the live
counters after the -Z (one-tick backward dip).

rexport.c: skip the push when health.json is >3min stale (collector crashed
without a clean stop) instead of POSTing a frozen snapshot as live; test bypasses.

web.c + defaults.c: raise reaper_fw_zone/zpol save cap 2048 -> RFW_LIST_MAX /
CKN_STR_MAX so the UI stops refusing a full zone matrix the engine accepts.

defaults.c: declare the 11 reaper_export_* keys (length class + factory default;
defaults apply on factory reset only, so existing configs are untouched).

reaper_shell.asp: nav-item geometry (height 38->40, icon 18->19, marker inset
7->8) standardized to Main_ReaperDash so the left rail is identical across pages.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
